---
description: Module controllers — ControllerFactory, naming, placement under src/modules/[name]/controllers.
globs:
  - "**/*.controller.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

- a controller should always live as part of a module, and be located at: `./src/modules/[name]/controllers/`
- a controller file must be named: `[name].controller.ts`
- never create a controller as a function. always as a class.
- a controller class should implement the `ControllerFactory` interface.
- a controller class always accepts `private readonly app: Application` as its first argument.
- a controller can only be instantiated by its domain module main class, under which it lives.
- request validation DTOs live in a `dto/` folder next to the controller.
- a dto file must be named: `[verb]-[resource].dto.ts` (kebab-case). do not put `Schema` in the filename.
- a dto file exports a camelCase Joi object named `[verb][Resource]Schema` (e.g. `create-user.dto.ts` → `createUserSchema`).
- default is the request body. include the source in the name only when it is not body (e.g. `get-books-query.dto.ts` → `getBooksQuerySchema`).
